ious":"09:36:08","deltaSeconds":-267}}},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":23,"finishersRank":20,"finishRateRank":68,"winningTimeRank":21,"winningTimeRankDir":6,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenRecords":["up"],"womenPreviousRecord":{"time":"06:32:56","holder":"Frith VAN DER MERWE","year":1988,"type":"up"},"womenHeroicSecond":{"name":"Maria BAK","time":"06:24:08","athleteId":"BAB35012-BC3D-4DD9-AB6E-8907CBC40AE1","brokenRecord":{"time":"06:32:56","holder":"Frith VAN DER MERWE","year":1988,"type":"up"}},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1966,"mensWinner":"Tommy MALONE","mensTime":"06:14:07"}},"narrative":"The 1996 Comrades Marathon was the 71st running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 86.700 km. The race was held on Monday, 17 June. Conditions: Cool at start with thin cloud layer. A few drops of rain shortly after the start. Chilly breeze for most of the morning. Otherwise cool to mild all day. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nDmitri GRISHIN claimed the men's title in 05:29:33, ahead of Nick BESTER (05:30:48) and Alexei Volgin (05:32:21). Ann TRASON won the women's race in 06:13:23, followed by Maria BAK (06:24:08).\n\nAnn TRASON set a new women's up record of 06:13:23, surpassing Frith VAN DER MERWE's 06:32:56 from 1988. Women's runner-up Maria BAK's 06:24:08 also beat the previous women's record. Ann TRASON's 06:13:23 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1966 (Tommy MALONE, 06:14:07).\n\nFrom a field of 13,538 entries, 11,260 runners crossed the finish line (83.2% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 10,029 men and 1,231 women (10.9% female). The average finish time was 09:31:41.\n\nMedals awarded: 15 Gold, 901 Silver, 10,344 Bronze. 2,719 runners (24.1%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Francois SPRING in 10:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 1994, the field was 6.6% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 35% of the finishers, with 7,362 seniors (avg 09:24:35) and 3,897 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}